        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, an asphalt shingle roof typically costs between $14,000 and $20,000, while a metal roof ranges from $20,000 to $44,000+ (or roughly 2 to 3 times the upfront cost of asphalt depending on the material and system).",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "an asphalt shingle roof typically costs between $14,000 and $20,000, while a metal roof ranges from $20,000 to $44,000+"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
