            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Metal Shingles / Aluminum: $20,000 \u2013 $40,000 ($10 \u2013 $20 per square foot installed)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Standing Seam Panels: $24,000 \u2013 $44,000+ ($12 \u2013 $22 per square foot installed)."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Upfront Investment: Higher initial cost, often 2x to 3x more expensive than traditional asphalt."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Factors for Utah Homes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Weather: Metal roofs shed snow readily, which is great for heavy mountain and northern Utah snow loads, though it requires specialized snow retention systems (like snow guards or fences) to prevent dangerous avalanches of snow onto walkways or cars, adding to the total project cost .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Lifespan: Asphalt shingles typically last 15 to 25 years, whereas metal roofing systems can last 50 to 75 years, offsetting the higher initial investment over time.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Specialized Labor: Fewer local residential contractors handle full metal installations compared to standard asphalt, meaning you may need a specialty contractor (such as B&D Architectural Metals LLC) which can impact labor pricing.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "HOA Rules: Always check your local Homeowners Association guidelines, as some Utah neighborhoods restrict exterior or metal panel finishes."
          }
        ]
      },
